abstract: >
  Slides for a half-day, browser-based workshop on making research software
  citable, discoverable, and reusable, co-presented by the UC OSPO Network and
  UC Carpentries and hosted by UCLA. Learners fork a demo GitHub repository and
  add an open source license, a CITATION.cff file, a versioned release with a
  DOI, and better documentation and metadata. Two decks: an introduction
  (why software citation matters, the UC OSPO Network, forking the demo
  repository) and "Improving Metadata and Discoverability". The slides
  accompany the lesson at https://ucospo.net/research-software-citable-discoverable/.
